# Bind the node workspace's VNC display to this session. `service = "browser"`
# is the built-in chassis service (127.0.0.1:5900); the page names it, and the
# chassis resolves the name — the page can never name a host or a port, so it
# cannot ask for the node's admin port directly. On success the chassis sends
# {"type":"attached"} and then the VNC bytes; a failure (the display is not up —
# call /ui/setup first) merges as workspace.error, which 300/connect-error
# reports.
WHEN .msg.type == "connect"
  EXEC "workspace://node/connect"
    WITH service = "browser",
         max_duration = "2h",
         into = "_connect"
